//  PETPORTS -- HUE LAMP MODULE EFFECT
//
//  THE RGB LAMP'S EFFECT WITH THE COLOUR ON A CLOCK. Same shape: an
//  animationConfig that declares the light, and a script that recolours it.
//
//  animationConfig IS WHAT GRANTS THE SCRIPT ITS animator, and that is not
//  incidental -- a status effect only gains access to the animator table when
//  this property is non-nil, so the light and the script that drives it have to
//  arrive together or the script has nothing to talk to.
//
//  ---- THE KNOBS ----------------------------------------------------------
//
//  ALL THREE ARE READ ONCE AT init, so retuning the sweep is an edit here and a
//  resocket, with no Lua touched.
//
//  huePeriod   SECONDS FOR A FULL TURN, AND ITS SIGN IS THE DIRECTION.
//              NEGATIVE runs the wheel widdershins, which is the shipped
//              default. A period rather than a rate because a period is a
//              number a person can picture. Eight is slow enough to read as a
//              colour rather than a strobe and fast enough to see move while
//              standing still. Only ZERO is refused -- that is a division by
//              zero, and it falls back to this default.
//
//  saturation  0 is white, 1 is the full wheel. Below about 0.6 the sweep reads
//              as a shifting white rather than as colour, which is a legitimate
//              thing to want from a lamp and a poor thing to get by accident.
//
//  intensity   BRIGHTNESS IN 0..255, AND THE ONLY BRIGHTNESS KNOB. This is a
//              LIGHT, not a sprite, so dropping it dims the room rather than
//              greying the unit. Stated in 0..255 because that is the unit the
//              other two lamps already use -- the plain lamp is authored at 140
//              and the RGB lamp defaults to it -- so the three are comparable
//              at a glance. 80 is deliberately dimmer than both: a colour that
//              moves draws the eye without having to be bright.
//
//  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//  scriptDelta 5 IS TWELVE UPDATES A SECOND, which against an eight second
//  period is a step of roughly two levels per tick on a ramping channel. Smooth
//  enough that the change reads as a fade. Lowering it costs work on every lit
//  unit in the fleet for a smoothness nobody asked for.
//
//  APPLIED PERSISTENTLY AND NEVER BY DURATION. The port calls
//  status.setPersistentEffects, which holds an effect for as long as it is in
//  the set. defaultDuration is unread on that path and is stated at vanilla's
//  lamp value so an effect applied some other way later behaves sanely.

{
	"name" : "petports_module_huelight",

	"effectConfig" : {
		"huePeriod" : -8,
		"saturation" : 1.0,
		"intensity" : 80
	},

	"defaultDuration" : 5,

	"scripts" : [ "petports_module_huelight.lua" ],
	"scriptDelta" : 5,

	"animationConfig" : "petports_module_huelight.animation"
}
